{"covers": [119978, 119977, 10124568], "first_publish_date": "December 28, 1989", "key": "/works/OL1966484W", "authors": [{"type": {"key": "/type/author_role"}, "author": {"key": "/authors/OL236174A"}}, {"type": {"key": "/type/author_role"}, "author": {"key": "/authors/OL1060314A"}}], "title": "The Extended Phenotype", "first_sentence": {"type": "/type/text", "value": "This is a work of unabashed advocacy."}, "type": {"key": "/type/work"}, "subjects": ["Gene expression", "Natural selection", "Genetics", "Evolution", "Evolution (Biology)", "Natuurlijke selectie", "\u00c9volution (biologie)", "Gene Expression Regulation", "Expressivit\u00e9 g\u00e9n\u00e9tique", "Genetic Selection", "G\u00e9n\u00e9tique", "Expression g\u00e9nique", "\u00c9volution", "S\u00e9lection naturelle", "Evolutie", "Genen", "Phenotype", "Life Sciences", "SCIENCE", "Biological Evolution", "G\u00e8nes", "Genes", "Gene expression--genetics", "Selection, genetic", "Qh375 .d38 1999", "1999 e-479", "Qh 375 d271e 1999", "576.8/2"], "description": {"type": "/type/text", "value": "By suggesting that individual organisms should be viewed as a single coherent unit, working to maximize their own reproductive success, the author explains that as these organisms are \"selfish\" they have the capacity to effect the body of another animal, so revolutionizing our views of adaptation."}, "latest_revision": 8, "revision": 8, "created": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2009-12-09T22:38:20.966423"}, "last_modified": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2025-07-07T18:17:39.375137"}}